# Trivy's baseline for the image scan in .github/workflows/ci.yml (the
# `docker` job scans every image before it is pushed and fails on a
# fixable HIGH or CRITICAL). These are the advisories that were already
# open against the production dependencies when the gate went in, by the
# id Trivy reports (the CVE where one exists, the GHSA otherwise).
# pnpm-workspace.yaml's auditConfig.ignoreGhsas is NOT the same list: it is
# empty by design, so `pnpm audit` gates on every advisory. Each line expires: past its date Trivy counts the
# finding again and the push fails, so fix the dependency and delete the
# line, or renew the date with a reason.


# guava 33.7.1 under the Eclipse JDT language server in the sandbox image
# (usr/local/jdtls/plugins/com.google.guava_*.jar; CVE-2026-102554, denial
# of service via unthrottled allocation during deserialization; fixed in
# 33.7.2). jdtls 1.63.0, the latest milestone, and the 1.64.0 snapshots
# bundle guava 33.7.1, so no jdtls build carries the fix yet. Bump
# JDTLS_VERSION in docker/Dockerfile once a milestone ships guava >= 33.7.2
# and delete this line. Not a pnpm dependency, so no auditConfig counterpart.
CVE-2026-102554 exp:2026-11-30
